This file stands in for whatever a Ravel package ships as its executable unit.

ADG-2 selects the mod execution and distribution model and is deferred to M3, so
no file here may be a dynamic library, a guest module, or a helper executable
without making that decision early. `schemas/package.schema.json` still requires
every target to declare at least one artifact, which `SPEC.md` §3.4 records as an
assumption inherited from the original draft rather than a settled contract.

So this package declares a file whose bytes are integrity-checked and whose
format is interpreted by nothing. `ravel-package` verifies the digest and does
not read the contents, and the declared role is `other` because calling it a
module or a library would name an execution model that does not exist yet.

For M2 the no-op mod runs as a plain Rust value the loader owns, built from
`test-mods/noop`. When M3 selects a mechanism, that decision replaces this file
and nothing else in the package has to change.
